{%- set enabled_toolsets_with_instructions = [] -%}
{%- set disabled_toolsets = [] -%}

{%- for toolset in toolsets -%}
  {%- if toolset.llm_instructions and toolset.status.value == "enabled" -%}
    {%- set _ = enabled_toolsets_with_instructions.append(toolset) -%}
  {%- elif toolset.status.value != "enabled" -%}
    {%- set _ = disabled_toolsets.append(toolset) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

# Available Toolsets
{% include '_fetch_logs.jinja2' %}

{% if enabled_toolsets_with_instructions|list %}
{%- for toolset in enabled_toolsets_with_instructions -%}
{% if toolset.llm_instructions %}

## {{ toolset.name }}
{{ toolset.llm_instructions }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}

# Disabled & failed Toolsets
{% if disabled_toolsets %}
The following toolsets are disabled or failed to initialize. Unless a different URL is given, each one's setup docs are at `https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/builtin-toolsets/<name before any slash>/` (e.g. toolset `foo/logs` → `https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/builtin-toolsets/foo/`).
{% for toolset in disabled_toolsets %}
{%- set default_docs_url = "https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/builtin-toolsets/" ~ toolset.name.split("/")[0] ~ "/" %}
* "{{ toolset.name }}" ({% if toolset.status.value == "failed" %}FAILED — enabled but misconfigured{% if toolset.error %}, error: {{ toolset.error }}{% endif %}{% else %}{{ toolset.status.value }}{% endif %}): {{ toolset.description }}{% if toolset.docs_url and toolset.docs_url != default_docs_url %} [setup: {{ toolset.docs_url }}]{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{% else %}
<no toolsets are disabled or failed>
{% endif %}

If you need access to a system you can't reach with your current tools:
  - Check the list above for a matching toolset. If its status is `failed`, tell the user and copy the error into your response. If `disabled`, ask the user to configure it and share its setup URL.
  - When users ask how to set up or give you access to a system (e.g. "How can I give you access to ArgoCD?"), point them to the matching toolset's setup URL above, or to https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/ if there is none.
  - If no toolset matches, tell the user you're missing an integration for that system, and that they can add one via an [HTTP connector](https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/api-toolsets/) (quickest for REST APIs — supports auth, endpoint whitelisting and response filtering), an [MCP server](https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/remote-mcp-servers/), or a [custom toolset](https://holmesgpt.dev/data-sources/custom-toolsets/).
